        "metadata": {
          "category": "stories",
          "minAge": 5,
          "maxAge": 12,
          "media": {
            "duration": 12499,
            "fileSize": 152456572
          },
          "abridged": false,
          "author": "Cressida Cowell",
          "description": "Hear the books that inspired the Dreamworks How to Train Your Dragon films.  \n\nTHE STORY BEGINS in the first volume of Hiccup's How to Train Your Dragon memoirs read by David Tennant...  \n\nHiccup Horrendous Haddock III, was a truly extraordinary Viking Hero. Warrior chieftain, awesome sword-fighter and amateur naturalist, he was known throughout Vikingdom as 'the Dragon Whisperer', on account of his amazing power over these terrifying beasts.  But it wasn't always like that.  In fact, in the beginning, Hiccup Horrendous Haddock III was the most put upon Viking you'd ever seen. Not loud enough to make himself heard at dinner with his father, Stoick the Vast; not hard enough to beat his chief rival, Snotlout, at Bashyball, the number one school sport and CERTAINLY not stupid enough to go into a cave full of dragons to find a pet...  \n\nListen to the rest of Hiccup's exploits in the rest of the series and check out the all-new Hiccup website at www.howtotrainyourdragonbooks.com. It's the place to go for games, downloads, activities and sneak peeks!",
          "audioPreviewUrl": "https://audio-previews-media.api.yotoplay.com/audio-previews/c2ac1595563a9857899a22457c1b13c0c963f359d4e88e8fb99f3d76def24d80/YYsddwlueyEkDZNzeBYMpydWOSRZ157Ch1lZWD2te2U.mp3",
